\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Drawn to the cross which Thou 
\par hast blessed
\par With healing gifts for souls distressed,
\par To find in Thee my life, my rest:
\par Christ crucified, I come!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Stained with the sins which I have
\par wrought
\par In word and deed and secret thought,
\par For pardon which Thy blood hath bought:
\par Christ crucified, I come!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Weary of selfishness and pride,
\par False pleasures gone, vain hopes denied,
\par Deep in Thy wounds my shame to hide:
\par Christ crucified, I come!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thou knowest all my griefs and fears,
\par Thy grace abused, my misspent years;
\par Yet now to Thee, for cleansing tears:
\par Christ crucified, I come!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. I would not, if I could, conceal
\par The ills which only Thou canst heal,
\par So to the Cross, where sinners kneel:
\par Christ crucified, I come!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Wash me, and take away each stain,
\par Let nothing of my sin remain,
\par Fro cleansing, though it be through pain:
\par Christ crucified, I come!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. To be what Thou wouldst have me be,
\par Accepted, sanctified in Thee,
\par Through what Thy grace shall work in me:
\par Christ crucified, I come!
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

